1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born March 30? 1896?(9 yrs old when arrived in US 1905 w/ her Gma Mine Steinberg)
2 CONT
2 CONT Died July 25, 1968
2 CONT
2 CONT From Harold Wyzansky:
2 CONT
2 CONT I added my grandmother's (your ggm) name and ran it back the two more generations that I know about. You actually have a bit of an error there because my father and your grandmother were half-siblings with different fathers so som
2 CONC ehow the box would have to be split to show multiple descent. Your grandmother's maiden name was Mintz. I don't know what her father's name was but he apparently a relative of your ggm as her mother's maiden name was also Mintz. T
2 CONC hey were divorced shortly after your grandmother was born and then your ggm came here leaving the baby in Lithuania with her mother. Your gggm, Mina, came here in 1907 to deliver your grandmother and then moved to Palestine where 
2 CONC she died and is buried on the Mount of Olives.
2 CONT
2 CONT ADDED A FEW DAYS LATER:
2 CONT
2 CONT Regarding what I told you about your grandmother, I am enclosing the page from ellisisland.org showing the arrival of Mine Steinberg and her "daughter" Mere, age 9, in 1905. Mine lied about her age and was really 68 and your grand
2 CONC mother's grandmother. I had found my grandmother in the 1900 census and always wondered why it showed her living without her daughter. Now I know it was because she was back in Europe. I have not found my grandmother's arrival rec
2 CONC ord. She may have come in at a different port than New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, my mother's maiden name was also Mintz. Your grandmother told me that my mother's father had known her father in Europe and they were not related despite have the same last name and both being from Lithuania.
